==============================================================================
EXAMPLE 2  (p.18-20):  R = F_9[x1,x2]/<t1,t2>
==============================================================================
  F_9 = F_3(w), w^2 + 2w + 2 = 0;  w = 7
  t1 = [7, 1, 1]  (x^2 + x + w)
  t2 = [2, 5, 1]  (x^2 + w^5 x + 2)
  t1 irreducible over F_9: True
  t2 irreducible over F_9: True
  dim_F9 A = deg t1 * deg t2 = 2 * 2 = 4
  |A| = 9^4 = 6561
  idempotents of A: 4   primitive: 2
  => |S-hat| = N = 2

  Each component contains a root of t1, which has degree 2 over F_9,
  so each component has F_9-degree >= 2.  Sum of degrees = dim_F9 A = 4,
  and there are 2 components => each has degree exactly 2.
  A ~= F_81 x F_81.   |F_9^N| = 9^2 = 81

  CONTRADICTION CHECK:  |A| = 6561  vs  |F_9^N| = 81
  psi : A -> F_9^2 cannot be injective, hence not bijective.

  Factorisation of the constacyclic moduli (checked against p.19):
    x^7 - 1  factors (deg, multiplicity): [(1, 1), (3, 1), (3, 1)]
    x^7 - w^2 factors (deg, multiplicity): [(1, 1), (3, 1), (3, 1)]
    g1 = x^3 + w^3 x^2 + w^5 x + 2 divides x^7-1 : True
    g2 = x + w^2 divides x^7 - w^2                : True
    deg g1 = 3, deg g2 = 1

  Theorem 8 as printed gives   sum_S (n - deg g_S)      = 10
  With |S(nu)| = 2 per component: sum_S |S| (n - deg g_S) = 20
  => the printed hull dimension 0 is unaffected (each term is 0),
     but the CODE dimension is 20, not 10.

  direct computation of dim_F9(A*g) by rank: 20   (primitive idem: 2)
  claimed code length nN = 7*2 = 14
  dim_F9 C = 20  >  nN = 14 ? True

