EXAMPLE 3  (p.20-21):  R = F_25[x1,x2]/<t1,t2>
==============================================================================
  F_25 = F_5(w), w^2 + 4w + 2 = 0;  w = 21
  t1 = x^2 + x + w^13 irreducible: True
  t2 = x^2 + w^3 x + 1 irreducible: False
  dim_F25 A = 4;  |A| = 25^4 = 390625
  two components, each of degree >= 2, summing to 4 => A ~= F_625 x F_625
  N = |S-hat| = 2 ;  |F_25^2| = 625  vs  |A| = 390625

    x^13 - 1  factor degrees: [1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2]
    x^13 - w^8 factor degrees: [1, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2]
    deg g1 = 3, deg g2 = 1
    g1 divides x^13-1 : True
    g2 divides x^13-w^8: True

  printed formula: 22 ; correct: 44
  direct computation of dim_F25(A*g) by rank: 44
  claimed length nN = 26 ; dim_F25 C = 44 > 26 ? True

